diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index 1b09cc68d..6d20deffe 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -110,3 +110,11 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - full-gate: Left out of bin/harness check: system tests (bin/harness test-system, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), the Bazaar non-ASCII test (needs the en_US.ISO8859-1 locale), bundle audit (needs network), and the PostgreSQL/MySQL and Ruby 3.3/3.4 matrix. The upstream workflows tests.yml and linters.yml still run all of them.
 - ci: The uw-harness package is not published on npm (npx -y uw-harness returned 404 here), so the new harness.yml workflow will fail until it is published. The gates were checked with the local build of uw-harness (check passes) and run directly from a clean shell.
 - deploy-explicit: Without human answers, docs/deploy.md and docs/observability.md keep open TODO blocks, so these two checks stay partial.
+
+## 2026-11-01: wiki toolbar syntax moved to the browser (#43259)
+
+What changed: the server no longer renders the syntax of the wiki toolbar buttons. `Redmine::WikiToolbar` subclasses only give `format_name` (`common_mark` or `textile`) and `groups` of button names; the base class renders spacers between groups, `data-wiki-toolbar-format-value` on the root, `wiki-toolbar#apply` with `data-wiki-toolbar-button-param` for normal buttons, `toggleMenu` for `table` and `precode`, `insertPrecode` with `data-wiki-toolbar-lang-param` for each language, and one generic `keydown->wiki-toolbar#shortcut` action. Shortcut keys (b, i, u) are in `Redmine::WikiToolbar::SHORTCUTS`. The syntax of each format (buttons, table cells, code block) is the exported `formats` object in `app/javascript/controllers/wiki_toolbar_controller.js`.
+
+What I learned: Stimulus key filters such as `keydown.ctrl+b` require the exact set of modifiers, so the generic `shortcut` action checks itself that only Ctrl (Cmd on macOS) is pressed, to keep the old behavior (Ctrl+Shift+B does nothing). `bin/rails` uses the macOS system Ruby 2.6 unless PATH contains the Homebrew Ruby; `bin/harness` fixes PATH only for its own tasks. The `frontend-stimulus` skill mentions `app/javascript/wiki_formatting/`, which does not exist.
+
+What is left: a plugin text formatter that uses the toolbar must now add its syntax to `formats` in JavaScript; there is no documented extension point for that yet. The system tests (`test/system/wiki_toolbar_test.rb`, `test/system/keyboard_shortcuts_test.rb`) pass locally with headless Chrome, but `bin/harness check` does not run them.
